3660-- Symptom: backup/migration work finishes but Codex still uses the old provider path, or someone tries to use `/Api_subscribe` as the API base. Cause: deploy state and client config were conflated. Fix: inspect `~/.codex/config.toml`, point `base_url` at the server root, and keep `/Api_subscribe` only as the browser landing page [Task 1]
3661-- Symptom: cleanup removes the wrong thing after deployment. Cause: rollback tags or uploaded backups were treated as permanent. Fix: if the user says they are unnecessary, delete only the temporary artifact/tag and leave the working image/runtime intact [Task 1]
3662-- Symptom: a host deploy or worker retune creates duplicate app containers. Cause: the wrong Compose project name was used. Fix: inspect the live project name first and recreate only that project [Task 1]
3663:- Symptom: a deploy creates a transient `repo-app-1` or otherwise touches the wrong stack. Cause: the Compose project identity was not pinned before running `docker compose up`. Fix: inspect the live project name first, then recreate only the intended project/container [Task 1]
3664-- Symptom: an LCO uninstall request gets buried under ongoing indexing or planning work. Cause: tooling investigation outruns the explicit user request. Fix: stop auxiliary LCO work, locate binaries/processes/DB paths, and execute the uninstall path first [Task 4]
3665-- Symptom: LCO cleanup claims success but new derived event-content rows or forced-start behavior keep appearing. Cause: the wrong env variable shape was used or active LCO rules were left behind. Fix: remove the active package/DB/rules entirely, and if temporary diagnostics are ever unavoidable, use `LCO_EVENT_CONTENT` / `LOO_EVENT_CONTENT` instead of bare `EVENT_CONTENT` [Task 4]
3666-- Symptom: direct upstream/account probes pass but public `/responses` returns 503. Cause: upstream success does not prove Sub2API routing, listener, account selection, or completed image deployment. Fix: inspect container state/logs, port binding, `/health`, and two-hop normal plus SSE responses before scheduling account 5 or binding it to a production group [Task 1][Task 5]
